Debug.Assert(OLD(x) + y = x);
</code>

In the provided C# code, there is an Assert statement that follows a comment starting with "@@@". The Assert statement accesses the value of a variable (x) at the beginning of the function, then adds a value (y) to it. If the condition in the Assert statement is true, the program would continue running without any issues, otherwise, an AssertionFailedException would be thrown. In this case, the Assert statement is checking if the original value of x plus the value of y equals the current value of x.
Here, the Assert statement doesn't check if some condition is met about the ArrayList class instance, as it is missing the context of the specific function where this Assert statement is used. Without a function context or a specific function, creating specific Assert statement is difficult as the intent and usage depend on the ArrayList methods and data.--------------------